n, named after New Hampshire’s royal governor Benning Wentworth, was in the southeastern part of what is now Vermont, only a short distance from the seat of New York’s government in Albany. The tavern was built around 1769 and featured a sign with a stuffed catamount or mountain lion.</p><p class="source"><strong>Source:</strong> Stereograph #B7.32—Silver Special Collections Library, University of Vermont.
</p></figcaption></figure>
